					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "VIDEO PLAYER\n\nThe Video Player node reads a video resource type and allows playback of that resource.\nThe video resource can be assigned through the node panel, Video Resource node or the Video In node.\n\nThe general operation of the node is very similar to how clips are played back in Arena\/Avenue.\nTriggers can be sent to start, stop, pause, rewind or restart the clip.\nPlaymodes like loop, play-once and bounce as well as speed controls are available too.\n\nBesides these basic controls the Video Player node has tons of hidden parameters for you to tweak. To access these: right click the node and navigate to 'visibility'."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 229.445098876953125,
					"width": 1104.5257568359375,
					"x": -344.071258544921875,
					"y": -29.927703857421875
				},
