			"81": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "EXAMPLE 2: GETTING WACKY\n\nIn this example we're utilizing a lot of the hidden parameters like the in-and-out point that let you trim the clip.\nSeek is used to scroll to a given spot in the video.\nCombining these parameters opens up a lot of creative doors like to this wacky auto-scratcher.\n\nAlso take note of the \"End Reached\" parameter.\nThe outlet sends a trigger when the clip is finished.\nThis allows you to chain multiple Video Players together or trigger something else in your patch, this outlet also plays very nicely with the Timeline node, which has the same \"End Reached\" parameter."
					}
				},
